- **Role:** Designated temporary security owner (Gemini 4 Argon High via AGY, replacing Opus until available again). This output is a **SECURITY AUTHOR proposal only**—it is not an independent audit, adoption, schema freeze, or decision vote. No tools, file edits, commands, browsing, or subagent delegations were executed.
- **Authority & Boundaries:** Native authority remains **zero** (`0`). All U0–U7, M1–M17, MC/SP/G, ZR/MNR/OSR, ACTUS, DeFi, and composition gates and counters are unchanged and remain open.
- **Schedule Separation:** `sherlock-k-a/1` (Candidate A K reference), `sherlock-quint-a/1` (Candidate A Quint reference), and `sherlock-helper-microstep/1` (Candidate B) remain strictly separate. Nothing here adopts or freezes Candidate B or transfers properties across profiles without a proved differential predicate (`OSR-1014-02`).
- **Untrusted Consumer Exclusion:** Existing Opus `dc0d7a44` source approval excludes untrusted consumers. This patch **does not** make `mori_core::sherlock` safe for untrusted inputs. H1 full host bounding (wall-clock time, heap allocation, $O(n)$ list/environment cloning, and native call-stack recursion bounds over deep `Expr`/`Tree` values) remains **open** and blocks CLI, LSP, MCP, `/1` or `/2` source adapters, and any network-reachable consumer.
- **Trace Invariance:** Executable `Machine` transitions, charges, rule line numbers, and existing normal oracles (`N01`–`N06`) are completely unchanged.

